<title>INDONESIA: TABLE-BDNI H1 net more than doubles.</title>
<headline>TABLE-BDNI H1 net more than doubles.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>			   (in billlion rupiah except per share)</p>
<p>    Net income			 160.477    vs	73.86</p>
<p>    Earnings per share (rupiah)    56	 vs	 26</p>
<p>    Total interest income	1,276.752    vs    896.492</p>
<p>    Net interest income	    307.218    vs    186.953</p>
<p>    Net income from operations   226.809    vs     99.367</p>
<p>    Non-operating income	     4.509    vs	6.485</p>
<p>    Tax provision		     70.660    vs     31.892</p>
<p>    Subsidiary interest		(.181)   vs	(.096)</p>
<p>NOTE: The results were audited. PT Bank Dagang Nasional Indonesia is one of the country's largest privately-owned banks.</p>
